{"obsah":"<p><strong>1/8 – Village festival exhibition – Třtěnice</strong></p>\n\n<p>Right after getting back from holiday, Vlasta packed the car, the trailer and his colleague Lukáš Valný and set off for Třtěnice to show the local boys how to ride a bike over obstacles. At first it looked like rain, but luckily they have it all figured out in Třtěnice and we rode under a roof that fitted the trailer and the obstacles. The turnout wasn't bad and you could see they have a promising biking community there that cheered us on.</p>\n\n<p><strong>2, 4, 8, 9/8 – Coaching, coaching, coaching and a kids' camp – Říčany area</strong></p>\n\n<p>A series of individual lessons flowed into the preparation of our August kids' camp, which was blessed with good weather and a great group of boys who flew around like their lives depended on it. Unfortunately Vlasta, Lukáš and Mára couldn't take part in the camp directly because of work commitments, but Lukáš at least took care of the technical side of the event and Vlasta did a small exhibition for the kids and parents at the end. All the more we could watch how much the boys progressed in those few days under the guidance of Katarína Tóthová and Matěj Bedrník.</p>\n\n<p><strong>13/8 – Day camp exhibition – Prague Počernice</strong></p>\n\n<p>A fellow biker remembered seeing us at an exhibition and asked if we could show something to the kids at their camp. A group of young boys and girls in the middle of the forest at a gamekeeper's lodge, on bikes all week, already had a solid programme, so instead of a classic exhibition Vlasta did more of a workshop explaining technique – but there was a bit of hopping over obstacles too.</p>\n\n<p><strong>14, 15/8 – Exhibition at the chateau – Bílé Poličany</strong></p>\n\n<p>When a village celebrates 750 years, it knows how to go all out, so the local chateau and park actually became a festival of local clubs, concerts by Czech bands and other attractions. Martin Šimůnek, Čihi and Lukáš Valný got to entertain over 500 people in front of the main stage, and judging by the feedback it hopefully went well. It was great that a few former Trial riders (now bikers) came for a chat, and apparently it inspired them to maybe bring their Trial bikes back out into the light. We topped off the weekend with double individual coaching on the trails and in the Tehov park, and at an Enduro training session with Petr Jeřicha there was a chance to test the new POC Kortal helmet from Levelsportkoncept. Simply put, there was plenty going on in those two days.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F08%2FIMG_0373.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F08%2FIMG_0373.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"193277\" data-link=\"https://bikeskills.cz/?attachment_id=193277\" class=\"wp-image-193277\"/></a></figure></li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F08%2FIMG_0375.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F08%2FIMG_0375.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"193279\" data-link=\"https://bikeskills.cz/?attachment_id=193279\" class=\"wp-image-193279\"/></a></figure></li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F08%2FIMG_0379.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F08%2FIMG_0379.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"193283\" data-link=\"https